cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Ferrotensor in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Ferrotensor: LoRA fine-tuning in Rust on portable GPU APIs through wgpu"
abstract: >-
  Ferrotensor is a Rust machine learning framework that trains and fine-tunes
  models through wgpu (Vulkan, Metal or DX12) with hand-written WGSL kernels
  and no CUDA toolchain. It runs LoRA fine-tuning of Llama-style language
  models from 135M to 1.7B parameters. Its LoRA loss and gradients are checked
  against PyTorch autograd in CI, and it writes adapters in the PEFT format.
  It has been tested on an NVIDIA A10G, an Apple M2 and software Vulkan;
  other GPUs are untested.
